{% extends "base.html.j2" %}
{% block content %}
<h1>Top PyPI Dependents</h1>
<p class="lede">Which PyPI projects does the rest of PyPI actually depend on? This ranks
projects by the number of other projects that declare a dependency on them, refreshed
monthly.</p>

<svg class="ornament" width="120" height="16" viewBox="0 0 120 16" fill="none"
    stroke="currentColor" aria-hidden="true">
  <path d="M0 8h46" stroke-width="1"/>
  <path d="M52 8c4-6 12-6 16 0-4 6-12 6-16 0z" stroke-width="1"/>
  <path d="M52 8h16" stroke-width="0.6"/>
  <path d="M74 8h46" stroke-width="1"/>
</svg>

<h2>How it is counted</h2>
<ul>
  <li>One release per project &mdash; the highest final release by PEP&nbsp;440 ordering,
      falling back to the highest prerelease for projects that have only prereleases.</li>
  <li>The headline number counts distinct projects declaring an <em>unconditional runtime</em>
      dependency. Dependencies gated behind an <code>extra</code> are counted separately, in
      the &ldquo;incl. extras&rdquo; column. That distinction matters: roughly 37% of all
      declared edges are extras-gated, which is why an unfiltered count puts test tooling
      above numpy.</li>
  <li>Names are normalized per PEP&nbsp;503, so <code>Zope.Interface</code> and
      <code>zope-interface</code> are one project.</li>
  <li>Only projects still live on PyPI are ranked, and only live projects count as
      dependents.</li>
</ul>

<h2>Known limitations</h2>
<ul>
  <li>Yanked releases cannot be excluded. The source table carries no yank status, and
      determining it would take one request per project.</li>
  <li>Only declared dependencies count. Transitive dependencies are not resolved.</li>
</ul>

<h2>Data</h2>
<p>The full ranked list is committed as JSON to the
<a href="https://github.com/miketheman/top-pypi-dependents/tree/main/data">data directory</a>
of the repository, one file rewritten by each monthly run. The complete dependency graph is
published as a DuckDB database and a Parquet edge list on each
<a href="https://github.com/miketheman/top-pypi-dependents/releases">release</a>.</p>
{% endblock %}
